  "details": "I have cool effects I'd like to use on my avatar but it can come with a large performance hit. Currently players only have the option to hide the avatar after guessing which avatar is lagging their game, or work with the confusing safety system such that a fallback avatar is shown instead.\nI suggest there should be an option for avatar creators to respect the user's quality preference. It could be an integer animator parameter of the existing quality setting that exists in the menu, or it could be a new setting. The idea is that avatar creators could disable performance-heavy parts of their avatar based on the user's quality preference.",
